sub:Head {
  this: a np:Nanopublication ;
    np:hasAssertion sub:assertion ;
    np:hasProvenance sub:provenance ;
    np:hasPublicationInfo sub:pubinfo .
}

sub:assertion {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/genotype-substitution-time> a delphi:Concept, skos:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "The time N independent substitutions need lies between N/(M mu) and N/mu (Lean 4, kernel-checked)" ;
    dct:description "With M gene copies, mutation rate mu per copy per generation and fixation probability u between 1/M and 1, the expected time for N independent sequential substitutions lies between N/(M mu) and N/mu, and equals N/mu in the neutral case; a time below N/(M mu) is impossible even if every mutant fixed." ;
    dct:source "Proved in this project (lean/Delphi/Favored.lean) as an extension of the neutral case of Kimura (1962) to non-opposing selection; no paper states it in this form." ;
    skos:notation "N/(M mu) <= N/(M mu u) <= N/mu ; T < N/(M mu) => False" ;
    skos:definition """/-- With `1/M ≤ u ≤ 1`, the waiting time lies between `N/(M μ)` and `N/μ`. -/
theorem expectedWaitingTime_bounds (N : ℝ) (hN : 0 ≤ N) (M : ℕ) (hM : 0 < M) (μ : ℝ) (hμ : 0 < μ) {u : ℝ}
    (hu1 : 1 / (M : ℝ) ≤ u) (hu2 : u ≤ 1) :
    N / ((M : ℝ) * μ) ≤ expectedWaitingTime N M μ u ∧ expectedWaitingTime N M μ u ≤ N / μ"""^^delphi:lean4 ;
    schema:programmingLanguage "Lean 4" ;
    delphi:leanDeclaration "Delphi.Genotype.expectedWaitingTime" ;
    delphi:leanTheorem "Delphi.Genotype.expectedWaitingTime_bounds", "Delphi.Genotype.expectedWaitingTime_neutral", "Delphi.Genotype.too_little_time_rules_out" ;
    delphi:leanVerified "true"^^xsd:boolean ;
    skos:scopeNote "An upper bound on speed, and nothing more. It cannot say a trait had too little time unless the number of required substitutions is defined, which it is not for any wing claim in this project; independent sequential fixations with constant M, mu and u exclude linkage, standing variation and recombination of partial solutions by assumption." ;

    rdfs:comment "Status: kernel-checked (Lean 4 accepted the module with zero sorry and standard axioms only). Not expert-validated. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: Independent sequential fixations at Kimura's definition rate with constant M, mu and u: no linkage, no standing variation, no recombination of partial solutions; That the number of required substitutions is given. It is not defined for any wing claim here, which is why this bound eliminates nothing about the flying fish; Nothing about whether the required substitutions exist, are favoured, or produce the trait. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Genotype.lean>, <https://delphibio.org/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://delphibio.org/t/lean/> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/genotype-substitution-time> dct:conformsTo <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/genotype-substitution-time> ;
    delphi:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-genotype-substitution-time> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/evidence/lean-kernel-check-genotype-substitution-time> a delphi:EvidenceItem ;
    rdfs:label "Lean 4 kernel accepted Delphi.Genotype.expectedWaitingTime_bounds with zero sorry and standard axioms; it also rejected 1 deliberately broken variant(s) of this statement or its model" ;
    dct:description "Build receipt. Lean (version 4.35.0, x86_64-w64-windows-gnu, commit eb6cafb7290e8bd5f2937522d8d804f58f02bafc, Release); toolchain leanprover/lean4:v4.35.0; Mathlib v4.35.0 (56a005855ea17e0b0958f73ec801ae140b0a1679). lake build exit 0 in 5.3 s with 0 errors; 0 sorry in lean/Delphi/Genotype.lean (224 lines). #print axioms for Delphi.Genotype.expectedWaitingTime_bounds, Delphi.Genotype.expectedWaitingTime_neutral, Delphi.Genotype.too_little_time_rules_out: Classical.choice, Quot.sound, propext only (Lean's standard axioms; no sorryAx). Mutation evidence (lean/mutate.mjs, 2026-10-31T22:57:06.367Z): 1 deliberate change(s) to this statement or its model were each rejected by the compiler: [waiting-time-bounds-swapped] Statement swapped: the waiting time claimed to be at most N/(M mu) and at least N/mu, the reverse of the bound. False for every u strictly between the ends, so the proof must fail. Rejected with 5 error(s): Genotype.lean:195:9: error: invalid 'calc' step, left-hand side is Controls: 17 of 17 unmodified modules accepted by the same command." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/math-law/genotype-substitution-time> ;
    rdfs:comment "This evidence item establishes that the stated theorem follows from the stated model. Does not establish: anything about organisms. The theorem is exact inside the stated model and silent outside it. The assumptions it rests on, written in the module header and never proved, are: Independent sequential fixations at Kimura's definition rate with constant M, mu and u: no linkage, no standing variation, no recombination of partial solutions; That the number of required substitutions is given. It is not defined for any wing claim here, which is why this bound eliminates nothing about the flying fish; Nothing about whether the required substitutions exist, are favoured, or produce the trait. Kernel-checked is not expert-validated: no human expert has validated these statements. Whether the Lean statement faithfully renders the source is a separate assessment record, and so far only one assessor provider has run." ;
    prov:wasDerivedFrom <https://delphibio.org/t/lean/lean.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/mutations.json>, <https://github.com/fractastical/delphisci/blob/4ebb56add61de66744fe8b957ecd7c0bcecc8083/lean/Delphi/Audit.lean> .
}

